          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Higher symplectic geometry
            is the generalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+geometry"} symplectic geometry
            to the context of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
          %p It involves two kinds of generalizations:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
                generalizes from a 2-form to a form of arbitrary arity. This aspect is called
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multisymplectic+geometry"} multisymplectic geometry
            %li
              %p
                the base
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
                is generalized to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
                or
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebroid"} ∞-Lie algebroid
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+Lie+n-algebroid"} symplectic Lie n-algebroid
          %p
            In the full higher symplectic geometry both of these aspects are unified: a
            %em
              multisymplectic
              = succeed "-groupoid" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid+--+structures"} differential n-form on smooth ∞-groupoids
            satisfying some condition.
          %p
            Examples of higher symplectic geometries arise naturally as the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+topological+quantum+field+theory"} extended topological quantum field theory
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            = succeed "-multisymplectic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            that defines the theory.
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
              be an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebroid"} L-∞ algebroid
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-plectic+form"} n-plectic form
              or
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multisymplectic+form"} multisymplectic form
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              arguments on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
              is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
                  which is
                  = succeed "-linear" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  arguments):
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi W
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ;
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\omega \in  W^n(\mathfrak{a}) = \Omega^n(\mathfrak{a})
                        \\,;
              %li
                %p such that the contraction morphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ι
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi ω
                        %mo :
                        %mi T
                        %mi 𝔞
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi W
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\iota_{(-)}\omega : T \mathfrak{a} \to W^{n-1}(\mathfrak{a}) = \Omega^{n-1}(\mathfrak{a})
            %p in injective.
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
              is a Lie 0-algebroid (over a smooth manifold) then it is simply that
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔞
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a} = X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{a}) = \Omega^{\bullet}(X)
              is the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
              and an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
              is a closed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
              of positive degree.
            %p
              In this case an
              = succeed "-plectic" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
              is a closed
              = succeed "-form" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo .
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega(-,-,.\dots, -)
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              such that for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+field"} vector field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in \Gamma(T X)
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\omega(v,-,\cdots,-) = 0) \;\; \Rightarrow \;\;
                    (v = 0).
          %h2#applications Applications
          %h3#higher_chernsimons_theory Higher Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            induces an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi CS
                  %mo :
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝔞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S_{CS} : \Omega(\Sigma,\mathfrak{a}) \to \mathbb{R}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+calculus"} variation
            of that functional is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi CS
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Σ
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi δ
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\delta S_{CS} : A \mapsto \int_\Sigma \omega(\delta A, F_A, \cdots, F_A)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Therefore the condition that the invariant polynomial is
            = succeed "-plectic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi CS
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{CS}
            has no spurious global symmetries.
